{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Denominator.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Denominator.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"denominator denominator","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Denominator.md","fileName":"Denominator.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Denominator","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Fractions and Decimal Forms]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Fractions and Decimal Forms","Fraction","Common Denominator","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Denominator.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Denominator.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"denominator denominator","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Denominator.md","fileName":"Denominator.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Denominator","heading":"Denominator","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The denominator is the lower, nonzero component (n) of a [[Fraction]] (m/n). It specifies the number of equal parts into which a unit is divided and serves as the divisor in (m\\div n).\n\nThe condition (n\\neq0) is essential because division by zero is undefined. Fractions with different denominators can be compared, added, or subtracted by converting them to a [[Common Denominator]]. Increasing the denominator while preserving the same numerator generally makes each represented part smaller.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Fractions and Decimal Forms","Fraction","Common Denominator","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Denominator.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Denominator.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"denominator denominator","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Denominator.md","fileName":"Denominator.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes",